<title>USA: U.S. refinery copper stocks rose in Sept - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. refinery copper stocks rose in Sept - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refined copper stocks held by U.S. refineries rose to 43,800 short tons at the end of September from 43,700 short tons in August, said the American Bureau of Metal Statistics.</p>
<p>Commodity Exchange Inc copper stocks were 21,700 short tons in the month, down from 22,100 short tons in August.</p>
<p>Combined refinery and COMEX stocks fell to 65,500 short tons in September from 65,800 short tons in the previous month.</p>
<p>U.S. refined production rose to 161,500 short tons from an August tally of 154,400. U.S. crude output was 135,700 tons, up from 121,700 in August.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodity Desk, 212 859-1640</p>
</text>
